# t05_led_interp.ledc -- ALL SEVEN INTERPOLATION PREFIXES on LED cells.  ~57 s
# NOT therapeutic.  Feature family: compound-cell animation.
#
# The prefixes config_parser.c:1768-1803 implements, and nothing else:
#     >v            linear ramp to the NEXT same-bit entry's value
#     *v            quadratic (ease-in-out) ramp to the same target
#     ~v:e:p        sine      modulation, v<->e every p ms
#     ^v:e:p        triangle  modulation
#     /v:e:p        sawtooth up
#     \v:e:p        sawtooth down
#     _v:e:p        square
# LED compound cells: freq duty bright R G B phase attack.  (mask, env and
# jitter are NOT compound -- a prefix there is silently discarded.)
#
# A `>`/`*` ramp needs a LATER entry on the same mask bit that EXPLICITLY sets
# the same field; if that entry writes `-`, the firmware ramps to ZERO instead
# of holding (there is no present-bit check on the target).  Every ramp below
# has a real target for that reason.
#
# BRIGHTNESS MODULATION RANGE: all brightness LFOs swing 40..100 at RGB 255,
# i.e. effective drive 102..255.  That is entirely inside the linear region, so
# the LFO's measured shape is the commanded shape.  A session that breathes
# 8..22 (drive 16..44) is compressed at BOTH ends and UNEVENLY -- the dim end
# loses more -- so its LFO shape is distorted, not merely shallow.  Do not grade
# an LFO shape down there.
#
# lane A = mask 3 (capture ch4), lane B = mask 12 (capture ch3).
#
#
#
# CAPTURE-INTEGRITY CARRIER (audio ch15, 1900 Hz sine, hard LEFT, vol 40, from
# t=700 ms to the end of the file).  This is measurement scaffolding, not
# content.  A recorder can lose a block of frames mid-capture and still write a
# file of exactly the right length -- the missing TIME is simply absent -- and
# the frame-count check is blind to it.  Five such steps were found in one 665 s
# capture (~1 per 2.2 min), and one of them was written up as a firmware defect
# because BOTH optical sensors agreed on it: the whole recording had stepped.
#   python3 tools/avmeasure/captureintegrity.py rec.wav --carrier 1900 --audio-ch 1
# The tool needs a CONTINUOUS SINE: a session cycling square/saw/noise carriers
# gives ~369 us of phase noise against ~1 us for a sine, which inflates its
# self-calibrating threshold into a rubber stamp.  Hard LEFT so the RIGHT capture
# channel stays free of it for envelope and avsync work.  The marker window
# (0..600 ms) is not covered by this carrier; check it separately with
# --carrier 3000.
# CAPTURE-CHANNEL MAP used throughout sessions/test (see README.md):
#   capture ch1,ch2 = device headphone jack L,R   capture ch3 = photocell on
#   lane B's eye (LED3+LED4, mask 12)             capture ch4 = photocell on
#   lane A's eye (LED1+LED2, mask 3).
# --------------------------------------------------------------- sync marker
0     40 50 100 255 255 255 15
A 0   3000 0 70 0 1
600   -1 50 0 0 0 0 15
A 600 0 0 0 0 1

# ---- capture-integrity carrier: continuous 1900 Hz sine, ch15, hard LEFT
A 700 1900 -100 40 0 15 0 0

# ---- ISR TICK PRIMER.  The flicker gptimer is DELETED whenever no channel is
#      left running and the next activation re-derives its tick from the 1000 Hz
#      FLOOR, so the marker's `freq 0` stop at 600 ms RESETS it -- the 40 Hz
#      marker does NOT pin the tick.  Worse, an update on an already-running
#      channel never calls s_ensure_timer_and_task, so whatever the FIRST
#      post-marker block sets is what every later block gets.
#      This row keeps ONE channel alive at 40 Hz for the whole file, pinning the
#      tick at clamp(40*250,1000,10000) = 10000 Hz = a 100 us grid everywhere
#      below.  mask 16 = LED5, which neither sensor can see (-78 / -74 dBFS, the
#      noise floor), and brightness is 0 regardless, so it cannot contaminate a
#      measurement on any unit.  It raises LEDC_MASK_HIGH_BITS (info) by design.
1000 40 50 0 0 0 0 16 0 0

# ---- B1  1..13 s : RATE RAMPS.  lane A linear 6 -> 10 Hz, lane B quadratic
#      12 -> 7 Hz.  Targets are B2's freq values.  A swept rate is the one case
#      where the V-S4 lattice snap is deliberately skipped (there is no fixed
#      lattice while the period changes every cycle), so grade the sweep with
#      percycle's quadratic tracker, not with an edge-count.
1000 >6  50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0     # lane A: > linear   6 -> 10 Hz
1000 *12 50 100 255 255 255 12 0 0     # lane B: * quadratic 12 -> 7 Hz

# ---- B2  13..23 s : ~ SINE on brightness (lane A) and ~ SINE on duty (lane B)
13000 10 50 ~40:100:2000 255 255 255 3  0 0   # lane A: bright 40<->100, 2 s LFO
13000  7 ~25:75:2000 100 255 255 255 12 0 0   # lane B: duty 25<->75, 2 s LFO

# ---- B3  23..33 s : ^ TRIANGLE (lane A) and / SAW-UP (lane B) on brightness
23000 10 50 ^40:100:2000 255 255 255 3  0 0
23000  7 50 /40:100:2000 255 255 255 12 0 0

# ---- B4  33..43 s : \ SAW-DOWN (lane A) and _ SQUARE (lane B) on brightness
33000 10 50 \100:40:2000 255 255 255 3  0 0
33000  7 50 _40:100:2000 255 255 255 12 0 0

# ---- B5  43..53 s : ~ SINE on a COLOUR cell (lane A: G swings 0..255 so the
#      colour runs blue -> white -> blue while total drive stays >= 255 on B)
#      and a > duty ramp 20 -> 80 (lane B), whose target is the B6 entry.
43000 10 50 100 0 ~0:255:2500 255 3 0 0
43000  7 >20 100 255 255 255 12 0 0

# ---- B6  53..57 s : ramp target / settle.  Short on purpose: it exists to give
#      B5's duty ramp an explicit endpoint, it is not a measured block.
53000 10 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
53000  7 80 100 255 255 255 12 0 0

# ---- end
57000 -1 50 0 0 0 0 15
57000 -1 50 0 0 0 0 16                     # stop the tick primer too
A 57000 1900 -100 0 0 15 0 0            # stop the integrity carrier
